.TH CUL-KDE 1 "2026-06-27" "1.0.0" "MCP Servers"
.SH NAME
cul-kde \- KDE Plasma Wayland desktop control MCP server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cul-kde
[\fIdoctor\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cul-kde
is an MCP (Model Context Protocol) server that exposes KDE Plasma
Wayland desktop capabilities to LLM clients. It provides 18 tools
for screen capture, window management, input simulation, and
accessibility tree access.
.SH COMMANDS
.PD 0
.TP
.B doctor
Run environment diagnostics and readiness check.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version information.
.PD
.SH MCP TOOLS
On startup,
.B cul-kde
runs in MCP stdio server mode and advertises the following tools:
.PD 0
.TP
.B doctor
Environment diagnostics
.TP
.B screenshot
Capture screen / window / region
.TP
.B list_windows
List all managed windows
.TP
.B focused_window
Get the currently focused window
.TP
.B activate_window
Activate a window by UUID
.TP
.B click\fR, \fBdrag\fR, \fBscroll
Pointer input simulation
.TP
.B press_key\fR, \fBtype_text
Keyboard input simulation
.TP
.B perform_action\fR, \fBset_value
AT-SPI accessibility actions
.TP
.B set_clipboard\fR, \fBget_clipboard
System clipboard via Klipper
.TP
.B list_apps
List accessible applications
.TP
.B get_app_state
Screenshot + AT-SPI tree snapshot
.TP
.B setup_accessibility
Enable AT-SPI accessibility bus
.TP
.B setup_window_targeting
Verify KWin window targeting
.PD
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B cul-kde
returns 0 on success, 1 on failure.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_SESSION_TYPE
Must be \fIwayland\fR.
.TP
.B KDE_SESSION_VERSION
Must be set (KDE Plasma session).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/udev/rules.d/99-uinput.rules
udev rule for /dev/uinput access
.TP
.I /etc/modules-load.d/uinput.conf
Kernel module auto-load configuration
